      en: ["The site served as Ishanapura, the capital city of the Chenla Empire.", "There are more than 100 temples, most of them constructed from brick.", "UNESCO designated the site a World Heritage site on July 8, 2017.", "The name translates to 'The temple in the richness of the forest'.", "Several temples feature an octagonal shape, which is rare in Khmer design.", "The Prasat Sambor group is the oldest of the three main temple clusters."],
